    "created_at": "2015-10-23T04:44:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-23T04:44:06Z",
    "body": "While I'm at it, both of those definitions include the HTML comment \"<!-- don't mention that the handle is optional, since if omitted, the method does nothing -->\". What if I wrote that omitting the handle means nothing happens, for greater clarity? My thinking is, it might seem that it should raise an error if no handle is given, when it sounds like it should just do nothing.\n",
